commit 2869c19d5074e74346ec27e3dd67f3903425895e
Author: hailyn3 <hailyn3@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Wed Oct 21 17:49:30 2026 +0000

    fix(#1057): keep in-scope trashed actors in activity reports
    
    The access lists behind the dashboard and activity-log filtered through
    User's SoftDeletingScope, so a soft-deleted user inside the unit scope
    vanished from both audit surfaces together with every row they produced.
    
    - Add the declared `withoutGlobalScope(SoftDeletingScope::class)` form
      (via `User::query()`, no macro) to both dashboard `$userIds` builders
      and to `getAccessibleUserIds()`; the unit predicate is unchanged.
    - Eager-load the `user` relation through `ActorLabel::eagerLoadActor()`
      so `deleted_at` is present on the list and `showDetail()` read paths.
    - Label with `ActorLabel::for()` on the dashboard rows and the activity
      detail modal; the raw `سیستم` / `نامشخص` fallbacks are gone.
    - showDetail keeps its not-found contract for out-of-scope rows.
    
    The two `User::whereHas()` baseline entries are stale after the query
    rewrite; the regenerated baseline only drops them (0 additions).

diff --git a/resources/views/livewire/activity-log/index.blade.php b/resources/views/livewire/activity-log/index.blade.php
